Title: 0007-aros-renderer-no-sticky-hint
Repository: grafx2
Base-Commit: f84cb09dc59d706d6e7b28778b01ba911f52298c
Requires: 0006-aros-exclusive-dos-lock.patch
Author: aros-grafx2 project
Date: 2026-09-20
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: AROS SDL2 renderer creation.

Problem:
  The AROS software-renderer path set SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER to software before CreateRenderer. That hint would still be set if software creation failed, so the declared accelerated fallback could not actually run.
Solution:
  Create the software renderer with SDL_RENDERER_SOFTWARE only, without the sticky hint, so a failed software create can still try accelerated.
Validation:
  2026-09-20 AROS One x86_64 ABIv11 under QEMU: GrafX2 2.9 opened
  with skins after this patch (software CreateRenderer succeeded). The
  accelerated fallback was not reached. Evidence:
  docs/attachments/2026-09-20-lock-ilbm/instance-a.png.
Removal:
  Keep the unsticky software-first CreateRenderer until an accelerated
  renderer survives GFX2_UpdateRect.

diff --git a/src/sdlscreen.c b/src/sdlscreen.c
index 64cf618a..2baf3fb4 100644
--- a/src/sdlscreen.c
+++ b/src/sdlscreen.c
@@ -133,11 +133,12 @@ static SDL_Renderer *GFX2_CreateRenderer(SDL_Window *window)
   // AROS SDL2 can return a non-NULL accelerated renderer that then dies in
   // SDL_LockTexture / stdlib memremove on the first GFX2_UpdateRect.
   // GrafX2 already renders in software; present through SDL's software path.
-  SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER, "software");
+  // Do not set SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER: it would stick and block the
+  // accelerated attempt below if software creation failed.
   renderer = SDL_CreateRenderer(window, -1, SDL_RENDERER_SOFTWARE);
   if (renderer != NULL)
     return renderer;
-  GFX2_Log(GFX2_WARNING, "software SDL renderer failed (%s), trying default\n", SDL_GetError());
+  GFX2_Log(GFX2_WARNING, "software SDL renderer failed (%s), trying accelerated\n", SDL_GetError());
 #endif
   renderer = SDL_CreateRenderer(window, -1, SDL_RENDERER_ACCELERATED | SDL_RENDERER_PRESENTVSYNC);
   if (renderer != NULL)
